  "summary": "Strict application of boosted decision-tree ensembles to battery remaining life is found in four papers. [V0087] uses GridWatch and reports AUROC 0.88; [V0086] uses ToxiBench and reports test MAE 0.81; [V0085] uses CellLife and reports accuracy 0.74; [V0088] uses ProtMap and reports F1 0.60. These results should not be pooled because AUROC, accuracy, and F1 are higher-better while MAE is lower-better, and the datasets differ. The fifth required slot, [V0078], concerns battery remaining life on ToxiBench but uses self-attention encoder models with F1 0.94, so it is not direct evidence for gradient boosted trees.",
